          "quote": "## What changes in the working theory\n\nGDT795's “smaller local status/quality field” survives, but it is now narrower:\n\n- it is not one general visible barrel/clothing/facing vocabulary;\n- it is not yet one fixed planetary-status vocabulary;\n- it may be a copied layout convention whose realization is conditioned by\n  sign, page, ring and local template;\n- the rest of the label behaves more like a learned entry than a composition\n  of freely translatable roots.\n\nThe best next bridge is therefore not another global substring dictionary.\nIt is to take `AQABBA`, the three complete-family visual rivals and recurrent\nlearned entries into their already admitted running paragraphs, mask every\ninherited generic gloss, and ask whether an entire paragraph or record selects\none concrete domain interpretation better than its rivals. The F9 result can\nbe used as a fixed layout sensitivity, never as a result-chosen semantic key.\n",
